  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The full suite passes: 1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a child context inherited the parent's entire `default_map`. A subcommand like `foo` was therefore looking up its options in `{\"foo\": {...}}` instead of `{...}`. The fix is to inherit only the entry for the subcommand's name: `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`, which checks that `default_map={\"foo\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}` sets the `--name` default for subcommand `foo`.\n\nWhile adding it, I first put the test in the middle of `test_flag_default_map` by mistake. I caught that on the failing run and put the original test back unchanged.",
